WEBVTT

00:06.506 --> 00:08.341
[sweet airy music]

00:43.168 --> 00:46.379
[light cheeky music]

00:46.463 --> 00:48.506
[squirting]

00:55.138 --> 00:56.431
[chuckles softly]

00:57.098 --> 00:59.350
There's this phrase in The Art of War.

00:59.934 --> 01:02.145
"The best defense is a good offense."

01:02.729 --> 01:05.356
Um, but you know, I don't exactly agree.

01:05.440 --> 01:07.776
[sucks teeth]
It's already hard to defend yourself.

01:07.859 --> 01:09.110
You won't have any strength.

01:09.194 --> 01:11.946
So in my own opinion, the best defense

01:12.864 --> 01:14.115
is running away.

01:14.741 --> 01:15.867
UNG IN ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

01:15.950 --> 01:18.953
[Ung] I have a very long history
of running away.

01:19.037 --> 01:23.875
All right, the student to present
about his beloved family in third period

01:23.958 --> 01:25.001
is Choi Ung.

01:25.085 --> 01:26.711
Ung, are you ready?

01:27.796 --> 01:31.716
We will just take a short break first,
and then we will begin, okay?

01:31.800 --> 01:33.259
[all kids] Okay!

01:34.093 --> 01:35.887
[kids chatting]

01:35.970 --> 01:38.181
[quirky music]

01:43.978 --> 01:46.898
[teacher] Ung, come down. Come on!

01:46.981 --> 01:48.191
[student] Come down!

01:48.274 --> 01:49.984
[teacher] Ung, come down from that tree!

01:50.068 --> 01:51.528
[Ung] At quite a young age…

01:51.611 --> 01:54.572
Ung, come down from there, please.

01:54.656 --> 01:56.950
You could get hurt. You can't stay there.

01:57.033 --> 01:59.619
I won't let you do the presentation,
so come down.

01:59.702 --> 02:00.787
I mean it, I won't.

02:00.870 --> 02:03.373
See? Pinky promise.
I won't make you do it.

02:03.456 --> 02:06.501
- [Ung] …I tasted the sweetness of it all.
- [teacher] Come down, all right?

02:07.836 --> 02:11.548
UNG IN HIGH SCHOOL

02:11.631 --> 02:14.843
[Ung] Of course, I run away for my sake.

02:14.926 --> 02:15.969
[Ho] Choi Ung!

02:16.553 --> 02:19.055
That brat completely broke this thing.

02:19.139 --> 02:22.475
- You brat! Stop right there!
- [Ung] But also for the other person.

02:22.559 --> 02:24.018
Look at what you did, jerk!

02:24.102 --> 02:25.854
[Ung] I am buying time for them

02:25.937 --> 02:28.857
so that we can have
a calm conversation later.

02:30.567 --> 02:32.944
[Ji-ung] This cost 29,900 won!

02:33.027 --> 02:34.571
[panting]

02:34.654 --> 02:36.072
UNG IN UNIVERSITY

02:36.156 --> 02:38.116
[Yeon-su] Wait, I won't hit you!

02:39.284 --> 02:40.952
[both pant]

02:41.786 --> 02:42.996
And I won't yell at you.

02:43.580 --> 02:44.747
[pants]
So come here.

02:45.707 --> 02:47.667
[Ung] So that we can have
a calm conversation,

02:48.418 --> 02:49.752
I am buying time for them.

02:49.836 --> 02:50.879
Do you mean it?

02:51.838 --> 02:52.755
[exhales]

02:53.923 --> 02:55.049
Come here.

02:58.094 --> 03:00.096
[panting]
Stop right there!

03:02.015 --> 03:05.393
That doesn't mean
I always run from everything.

03:06.060 --> 03:09.188
- Is it because you're entering a marathon?
- Mm-hmm.

03:09.272 --> 03:11.316
[Ung] Yeon-su said that
if I do the half marathon,

03:11.399 --> 03:12.817
we'll wear matching rings.

03:12.901 --> 03:14.068
[sighs]

03:14.861 --> 03:16.696
She really is amazing, huh?

03:16.779 --> 03:17.947
[grunts]

03:18.031 --> 03:20.783
- Is she dating or babysitting you?
- [sucks teeth]

03:20.867 --> 03:22.702
She still doesn't know me well.

03:22.785 --> 03:24.203
I'm a man of my word.

03:24.996 --> 03:28.333
Hey, listen. I'm gonna give you
some tough training,

03:28.416 --> 03:30.293
so don't you dare go back on your word.

03:30.376 --> 03:32.211
We're running for an hour every day.

03:32.295 --> 03:33.421
Yeah, yeah. I know.

03:33.504 --> 03:35.381
A half marathon is a cake walk.

03:35.465 --> 03:37.258
I could probably
complete the full marathon.

03:37.926 --> 03:39.010
Eat my dust.

03:41.638 --> 03:42.722
[tuts]
Jeez.

03:42.805 --> 03:45.183
[upbeat music]

03:45.266 --> 03:46.517
[Ung chuckles]

03:47.352 --> 03:49.187
- [Ji-ung] Get going.
- [Ung] No.

03:49.270 --> 03:50.855
[Ung groaning]

03:51.856 --> 03:53.942
[Ung] No, I can't do this anymore.

03:55.109 --> 03:56.903
- [Ji-ung] Come on.
- [Ung] No!

04:00.323 --> 04:02.533
[quirky music]

04:08.248 --> 04:09.916
- [phone buzzing]
- [gasps awake]

04:11.501 --> 04:13.002
[buzzing continues]

04:14.462 --> 04:16.464
[groans]

04:20.426 --> 04:21.719
[grunts]

04:21.803 --> 04:24.347
[groans, sighs]

04:24.430 --> 04:25.765
INCOMING CALL
KIM JI-UNG

04:28.059 --> 04:31.813
[Ung] I make objective judgments
to make the best decision.

04:31.896 --> 04:33.356
INCOMING CALL
KIM JI-UNG

04:33.439 --> 04:35.608
[groaning]

04:37.902 --> 04:41.823
Right. I can just wear
matching rings with Ji-ung.

04:41.906 --> 04:43.032
Right. Right.

04:44.117 --> 04:45.952
[strained groans]

04:47.120 --> 04:49.372
[quirky music continues]

04:53.334 --> 04:56.337
So I'm not embarrassed about running away.

04:56.421 --> 04:59.674
UNG IN THE PRESENT

05:01.467 --> 05:02.760
[music fades]

05:07.015 --> 05:08.433
It's been way too long,

05:10.601 --> 05:12.186
we should be able to…

05:13.062 --> 05:14.647
ask each other "How have you been?"

05:16.065 --> 05:17.317
"How tough has it been for you?"

05:19.736 --> 05:22.238
"It's been tough for me."
We're allowed to say those things.

05:23.614 --> 05:25.033
[groans]
Damn it…

05:25.116 --> 05:27.493
[pensive music]

05:32.874 --> 05:35.418
I asked you
for a writer a long time ago, didn't I?

05:35.501 --> 05:37.045
Are you sending me one, huh?

05:37.128 --> 05:39.672
Well, about that, you know…

05:41.007 --> 05:42.425
[clears throat]

05:42.508 --> 05:45.428
I did my best to find one for you,
so don't blame me for this, okay?

05:45.511 --> 05:47.430
Everyone is working on something.

05:47.513 --> 05:49.849
Which means,
no one is available to send to you.

05:49.932 --> 05:51.017
So sadly…

05:51.517 --> 05:54.145
Hmm, anyway, good luck, all right.

05:54.729 --> 05:57.190
What's this? Who is it?
Why are you making such excuses?

06:04.197 --> 06:06.240
[sighs deeply]

06:06.324 --> 06:08.701
Come on in already.

06:08.785 --> 06:10.703
Are you just going to stand there all day?

06:11.829 --> 06:14.207
You know you're overqualified
to be working on this.

06:14.290 --> 06:16.292
So what are you doing in here, huh?

06:16.375 --> 06:18.294
- [Ji-ung] It's just a simple project.
- [sighs]

06:18.377 --> 06:20.630
You know what, I'll just get
one of the rookie writers to help.

06:20.713 --> 06:22.965
Why? Do you think I wanted to do this?

06:23.049 --> 06:26.677
Mr. Park was desperately
asking for my help.

06:26.761 --> 06:28.846
You said you were gonna work
on dramas now.

06:28.930 --> 06:31.390
- So just go and write one instead of--
- Well, I am.

06:31.474 --> 06:34.519
I hate it when people tell me to write
when I already am.

06:35.061 --> 06:36.813
I came here to clear my head a bit,

06:36.896 --> 06:39.440
so please, don't be so obvious
about hating me being here.

06:40.358 --> 06:43.736
- Are trying to have your way?
- That's what makes them great.

06:43.820 --> 06:45.404
I don't want you on this.

06:45.488 --> 06:48.908
- I…
- I saw the preview, and it was awful.

06:50.284 --> 06:51.953
[Ji-ung] Who said you could show her?

06:52.036 --> 06:55.414
Mr. Kim… what in the world
are you trying to film here?

06:55.498 --> 06:58.876
I don't get what you're trying to say
through these videos that you shot.

06:58.960 --> 07:01.212
What the hell has gotten into you?

07:01.295 --> 07:03.422
- Have you lost your touch?
- [Ji-ung] Okay, you know something,

07:03.506 --> 07:07.009
I'll take care of this myself,
so go the hell back to where you came from

07:07.093 --> 07:10.429
or go clear your head somewhere else
as long as it's away from me an my crew!

07:10.513 --> 07:11.472
[Chae-ran] Mr. Kim.

07:12.682 --> 07:13.724
[sighs]

07:13.808 --> 07:16.853
We're in a bad situation.
We really do need a writer.

07:17.895 --> 07:21.065
Well, I do have something to make up for.

07:22.358 --> 07:24.485
I won't be that stubborn this time.

07:26.237 --> 07:27.613
[sighs]

07:28.865 --> 07:29.907
[exhales]

07:35.997 --> 07:37.165
All right then…

07:39.167 --> 07:40.501
what is it you have in mind?

07:43.087 --> 07:46.424
I heard that the cast are your friends.
Is that why you were lazy?

07:48.009 --> 07:51.846
Well, honestly,
I was thinking of refusing this project.

07:53.055 --> 07:56.476
But as I kept watching,
I found something interesting.

07:56.559 --> 07:58.936
So I watched the documentary
from ten years ago.

07:59.020 --> 08:01.439
- So what?
- There seemed to be something

08:01.522 --> 08:04.066
going on between the two of them, no?

08:07.403 --> 08:10.364
There is no way
that you wouldn't have noticed that.

08:11.949 --> 08:15.411
If we write a story based on that,
it'd be quite a show.

08:15.495 --> 08:17.914
I don't want to make anything up.
[sighs]

08:18.539 --> 08:20.541
No, it actually felt like,

08:20.625 --> 08:25.338
like the camera was purposely trying
to ignore that part, you know what I mean?

08:26.547 --> 08:29.383
- But then, that was just me.
- Why would I do that intentionally?

08:29.467 --> 08:31.469
I was just trying
to film objectively and--

08:31.552 --> 08:33.679
[Min-gyeong] Then why the heck
would people film things?

08:33.763 --> 08:36.182
You can just let machines
do all the shooting then.

08:36.265 --> 08:40.228
My goodness. You really haven't
changed a bit, Mr. Kim.

08:42.230 --> 08:46.651
Well, at the very least,
you made the scenes look quite pretty.

08:47.401 --> 08:48.861
I'll just whip something up…

08:49.987 --> 08:51.572
based on them.

08:52.406 --> 08:54.492
[mysterious music]

08:59.956 --> 09:01.207
- Oh, hey, you're up.
- [Ung] Hey.

09:01.290 --> 09:02.792
We're having a party today, all right?

09:02.875 --> 09:04.252
Look behind you.

09:04.335 --> 09:05.628
[laughs]

09:05.711 --> 09:08.965
[Eun-ho] I put in so much effort
to prepare your debut anniversary party.

09:09.048 --> 09:10.174
[chuckles]

09:10.258 --> 09:12.426
Oh, right. Yeon-su's coming too
because we're filming.

09:12.510 --> 09:13.469
[chokes]

09:13.553 --> 09:14.637
[sighs]

09:14.720 --> 09:16.722
Now is there anyone else
I forgot to invite?

09:17.306 --> 09:18.891
Maybe someone like NJ would like to come.

09:18.975 --> 09:20.101
Like NJ, you know.

09:20.184 --> 09:21.394
Or just NJ.

09:24.188 --> 09:26.274
Right, Ji-ung said
he's coming early today.

09:26.357 --> 09:27.817
[groans]
I should prepare this.

09:30.152 --> 09:33.489
Ung! Ji-ung said he's coming over first
so go and get ready, okay?

09:33.573 --> 09:37.034
[Ung] By running away,
I'm not avoiding anything,

09:37.118 --> 09:38.828
 it's a reasonable decision.

09:40.663 --> 09:41.831
Okay.

09:42.915 --> 09:44.834
[light cheeky music]

09:52.425 --> 09:53.551
[Yeon-su] Running away?

09:56.887 --> 10:01.559
Running away from things is something
only cowardly people would do.

10:03.728 --> 10:05.062
[sighs]

10:12.987 --> 10:16.949
I've never run away from anything,
not once in my life.

10:19.118 --> 10:21.162
[light music]

10:22.913 --> 10:24.081
[groans]

10:24.165 --> 10:25.374
Sorry.

10:26.917 --> 10:28.836
Uh, I'm quite drunk right now, Ung.

10:31.422 --> 10:33.507
[light music continues]

10:35.801 --> 10:37.511
[deep sigh]

10:38.888 --> 10:43.559
Has all nothing more than
a pathetic excuse that they used.

10:43.643 --> 10:44.894
[sighs]

10:47.104 --> 10:48.272
Let's get some coffee.

10:51.359 --> 10:52.526
So then?

10:52.610 --> 10:54.487
[Min-gyeong] Have you read all my draft?

10:57.198 --> 10:58.574
I guess you haven't yet.

10:58.658 --> 11:02.745
I'm sure you wouldn't be making faces
after reading such an amazing draft.

11:02.828 --> 11:05.206
Sorry, but we can't film

11:05.289 --> 11:08.084
- this amazing story of yours.
- What? Why?

11:09.251 --> 11:10.252
[sighs]

11:10.336 --> 11:15.383
Mr. Kim. Don't you think it's a bit
too childish to reject my works like this?

11:16.092 --> 11:17.802
- They ran away.
- Who did?

11:17.885 --> 11:19.970
- The cast.
- Who exactly in the cast?

11:20.054 --> 11:22.014
- Choi Ung.
- [scoffs]

11:22.681 --> 11:24.558
Go get him then. It's no big deal.

11:24.642 --> 11:26.060
And Kook Yeon-su.

11:27.436 --> 11:29.063
[tense music]

11:29.146 --> 11:30.189
[sighs]

11:31.899 --> 11:34.610
EPISODE 7
CATCH ME IF YOU CAN

11:34.693 --> 11:40.366
CELEBRATION PARTY
CHOI UNG, KOOK YEON-SU

11:41.117 --> 11:44.203
ONE HOUR EARLIER

11:48.124 --> 11:50.251
[line trilling]

11:53.671 --> 11:56.424
I told you I called him several times.
It's useless.

11:56.507 --> 11:58.300
You said you were
with him this morning, right?

11:58.384 --> 12:01.971
Hm. He was here earlier,
but he just disappeared.

12:02.054 --> 12:04.432
Did you really not hear
anything from Yeon-su?

12:04.515 --> 12:05.766
Oh, you mean me?

12:06.684 --> 12:09.687
You see all these wine bottles?
These are the ones I brought.

12:09.770 --> 12:11.897
I went to the trouble
of closing my bar today,

12:11.981 --> 12:14.942
so I could attend this party.
And now what?

12:15.818 --> 12:17.403
Don't you think I'm a victim too?

12:17.486 --> 12:20.239
I get Choi Ung
would do something like this,

12:20.322 --> 12:22.158
but Yeon-su is not that irresponsible.

12:23.534 --> 12:25.870
You don't think maybe something
happened to them, do you?

12:25.953 --> 12:27.913
Didn't you take her home last night?

12:28.497 --> 12:30.458
Does she still have a hangover?

12:30.541 --> 12:33.002
- I remember she barely does.
- [line trills]

12:33.085 --> 12:34.503
I'll try calling her grandma.

12:36.881 --> 12:38.507
[sighs deeply]

12:38.591 --> 12:39.884
Hmm.

12:40.551 --> 12:43.804
- What? Is it Yeon-su?
- She did go AWOL.

12:44.763 --> 12:49.143
"I need some time to think.
Don't tell my grandma anything."

12:49.935 --> 12:52.771
Judging from that rude text,
it looks like she hasn't been kidnapped.

12:52.855 --> 12:54.440
[Eun-ho] Yeon-su went AWOL?

12:54.523 --> 12:57.151
- Why? What for?
- Now where could Ung be?

12:57.234 --> 12:59.612
Oh, you know the guy. He can be so simple.

12:59.695 --> 13:02.740
If we just look around the neighborhood,
we'll find him right away. Don't worry.

13:03.365 --> 13:05.910
Why is he suddenly doing this?

13:05.993 --> 13:08.245
The drawing show went well yesterday.

13:08.329 --> 13:10.706
- I really don't get it.
- [sighs]

13:10.789 --> 13:14.710
Isn't it a bit strange for them
to do this at the same time?

13:14.793 --> 13:17.838
I mean, maybe something happened
between the two of them.

13:19.215 --> 13:20.174
Don't you think?

13:21.342 --> 13:22.510
Or is it just me?

13:22.593 --> 13:25.262
No way. I didn't actually see them
together yesterday, though.

13:25.846 --> 13:29.517
Right. And Yeon-su came into my bar
right after it ended,

13:29.600 --> 13:32.061
and then she got drunk,
and then she went straight home.

13:32.144 --> 13:34.563
Ung was tired
and went to bed early last night too.

13:36.774 --> 13:40.027
[cheeky realization music]

13:41.612 --> 13:43.280
[rattling]

13:53.791 --> 13:55.084
[blows out breath]

13:55.167 --> 13:57.670
[Ung] Was I really drunk last night?

13:59.296 --> 14:00.464
No way.

14:00.548 --> 14:03.300
Did I take pills yesterday?

14:06.220 --> 14:07.513
Nope.

14:07.596 --> 14:11.308
Did I still cry
in front of Yeon-su regardless?

14:14.186 --> 14:15.145
[sighs heavily]

14:17.856 --> 14:19.900
[quirky music]

14:21.068 --> 14:22.111
[sighs]

14:22.611 --> 14:24.947
[leaves rustling]

14:27.032 --> 14:28.033
But…

14:28.951 --> 14:31.954
she probably won't remember anything
since she was drunk.

14:32.538 --> 14:33.622
[phone buzzing]

14:35.165 --> 14:37.209
[quirky music continues]

14:38.043 --> 14:39.628
GU EUN-HO

14:39.712 --> 14:42.923
[Eun-ho] You'll get caught anyway.
So just tell us where you are already.

14:43.007 --> 14:45.801
Is this because I asked you for a raise?
I'm not giving up, though.

14:45.885 --> 14:48.804
Are you with Yeon-su right now?
Why are you both suddenly going AWOL?

14:48.888 --> 14:50.139
[sighs deeply]

14:51.599 --> 14:52.433
[clicks tongue]

14:54.143 --> 14:57.146
[Ung] I'll avoid it for now
and think things through later.

14:57.229 --> 14:58.814
[blows out breath]

15:00.524 --> 15:02.526
[bright pensive music]

15:03.736 --> 15:04.987
[twig cracks]

15:07.740 --> 15:09.909
[Yeon-su] Well, I did expect this, but…

15:10.701 --> 15:12.453
There's nowhere for me to go now.

15:14.079 --> 15:17.666
What do people usually do
when they're in my situation?

15:22.171 --> 15:24.256
[bright music continues]

15:27.885 --> 15:28.844
Oh.

15:31.513 --> 15:33.432
I don't really have friends.

15:39.980 --> 15:42.191
I'm not running away.

15:42.274 --> 15:45.819
I'm just keeping my distance
until I can get my thoughts in order.

15:49.949 --> 15:51.867
This is so fun.

15:52.826 --> 15:53.911
Huh?

15:54.536 --> 15:56.413
The two of them ran away,
isn't that right?

15:59.708 --> 16:01.794
How exciting.
This is even better than I thought!

16:01.877 --> 16:04.338
Isn't it strange that they both went AWOL?

16:04.421 --> 16:06.048
A bit strange, yes.

16:06.131 --> 16:07.049
That's right.

16:07.925 --> 16:11.303
This is going to hit the jackpot.
Clearly, there must be something going on!

16:11.387 --> 16:14.223
I have to be able to film something
for it to hit the jackpot.

16:14.306 --> 16:16.600
And how can I do that
without any of the cast?

16:17.184 --> 16:18.978
What on earth has gotten into you?

16:19.061 --> 16:21.772
- You don't seem enthusiastic about this.
- What do you mean?

16:21.855 --> 16:24.733
When have you ever given up
just because the cast ran away?

16:24.817 --> 16:26.276
Remember what happened with Jukdo?

16:26.360 --> 16:27.653
Why would you bring that up?

16:27.736 --> 16:29.571
When you heard
that the whole cast went AWOL,

16:29.655 --> 16:31.782
you searched
the entire island for them, did you not?

16:31.865 --> 16:33.283
- Plus, that snake farm.
- [sighs]

16:33.367 --> 16:36.203
You ran around the mountain
looking for that snake that escaped.

16:36.286 --> 16:38.914
And now you're telling me that
you can't film just because of that?

16:38.998 --> 16:40.082
Even if I do find them,

16:40.165 --> 16:43.752
would I be able to film anything good
if I forced them to stay on camera?

16:43.836 --> 16:45.087
If you bring them back,

16:46.171 --> 16:48.298
make sure that
they can never run away again.

16:49.258 --> 16:51.385
[inhales]
Let's see…

16:52.886 --> 16:55.597
Would you prefer mountains or islands?

16:55.681 --> 16:56.849
Uh, what?

16:58.684 --> 17:00.227
Hey, you, Intern.

17:00.310 --> 17:02.980
[inhales]
What are my works most known for?

17:03.063 --> 17:05.149
Bringing out the primal emotions of people

17:05.232 --> 17:08.027
using limited space
in an unfamiliar environment.

17:08.110 --> 17:09.653
Say that simply.

17:10.529 --> 17:13.032
- Locking up the cast?
- [chuckles]

17:13.115 --> 17:15.451
The weather's nice. So let's go on a trip.

17:16.493 --> 17:18.829
Kidnap the cast,
and take them somewhere secluded,

17:18.912 --> 17:20.748
and then film them for about three days.

17:21.582 --> 17:22.666
[Min-gyeong] Okay?

17:24.918 --> 17:26.670
[Eun-ho] All right, all right,
don't worry.

17:26.754 --> 17:28.839
I'm doing my best to find him.

17:28.922 --> 17:31.508
Hmm. I'll call you once I find him.

17:31.592 --> 17:35.304
Oh, wait, there's a taxi. Taxi!
I'll just call you later, okay?

17:38.098 --> 17:40.142
- [chuckles]
- [quirky music]

17:41.810 --> 17:43.020
Thank you, Choi Ung.

17:44.271 --> 17:46.440
Dobby is free. Thank you so much.

17:52.112 --> 17:53.280
Oh, my gosh! What the?

17:53.989 --> 17:57.034
- I was here the whole time by the way.
- What are you doing here?

17:57.785 --> 17:58.619
I got hungry.

17:58.702 --> 18:02.289
You know, there's a lot of food here,
but there's nothing to eat.

18:02.372 --> 18:03.999
Wait, you didn't leave?

18:04.708 --> 18:06.877
- Nobody told me to.
- But everyone already left.

18:06.960 --> 18:08.295
My bottles are still here.

18:08.378 --> 18:10.422
I mean, shouldn't you
be looking for Yeon-su?

18:10.506 --> 18:11.507
What about you?

18:12.382 --> 18:15.469
Hold it, why are you
talking so casually to me right now?

18:15.552 --> 18:19.556
Oh, well, I strongly support and believe
in a hierarchy based on someone's age.

18:19.640 --> 18:21.683
- And I happen to be older than you.
- [gasps]

18:21.767 --> 18:23.936
So, you really don't know
where Ung is, huh?

18:24.019 --> 18:25.687
Oh, of course I do.

18:25.771 --> 18:28.315
It's obvious where he most likely went.

18:28.398 --> 18:30.400
He doesn't have any friends or hobbies.

18:30.484 --> 18:31.944
It's the same for Yeon-su.

18:32.027 --> 18:34.113
You think that's the reason
why they dated?

18:35.114 --> 18:37.324
I guess he does have
something like a hobby.

18:37.407 --> 18:39.034
It's obvious.

18:39.118 --> 18:41.245
Those two are together right now.

18:42.412 --> 18:44.873
Isn't this your first time
coming to this house, though?

18:45.457 --> 18:47.668
How come you're acting
like you own the place, huh?

18:47.751 --> 18:49.837
Well, I came here to have fun,

18:49.920 --> 18:51.713
and I did close my bar for this.

18:52.297 --> 18:53.882
[Sol-i] I can't just sit around.

18:56.468 --> 18:58.929
How about a party without them?

18:59.638 --> 19:01.557
[cheery music]

19:04.351 --> 19:05.269
Sol-i.

19:06.061 --> 19:07.271
You're such a genius.

19:08.021 --> 19:09.022
[music stops]

19:16.363 --> 19:18.365
[awkward music]

19:22.578 --> 19:24.872
[Ung] It feels like I've already come back

19:24.955 --> 19:27.583
only three hours after I ran away.

19:28.458 --> 19:31.420
[Yeon-su] I ended up
right in front of Ung again.

19:32.880 --> 19:34.047
Hi.

19:34.131 --> 19:35.090
[Ung] Okay, that's it.

19:35.174 --> 19:37.801
That's the worst thing
I said this entire year.

19:38.635 --> 19:39.887
Mm.

19:40.679 --> 19:41.597
[clears throat]

19:42.306 --> 19:43.473
Hey, so…

19:44.224 --> 19:45.434
What are you doing here?

19:48.270 --> 19:49.354
Oh.

19:50.480 --> 19:51.732
I thought you…

19:53.942 --> 19:56.028
were doing a celebration party today.

19:56.111 --> 19:57.362
What about you?

19:57.446 --> 19:59.406
Uh…
[sucks teeth]

19:59.489 --> 20:00.991
I wanted to get some rest.

20:02.659 --> 20:04.661
- [Ung] Mm.
- [light awkward music]

20:10.167 --> 20:11.543
[both sigh]

20:11.627 --> 20:13.253
This is really awkward, you know?

20:13.337 --> 20:15.672
Really? I feel fine, though.

20:16.673 --> 20:19.009
- Really?
- Mm-hm. I'm totally fine.

20:19.635 --> 20:21.511
Why on earth would we be awkward?

20:22.012 --> 20:25.307
Hmm. You must have decided
to pretend not to remember.

20:25.807 --> 20:28.185
- I don't know what you're saying.
- Hey, Kook Yeon-su.

20:28.977 --> 20:29.978
[deep sigh]

20:31.313 --> 20:33.273
All right, fine. It's awkward.

20:33.357 --> 20:35.192
I got drunk and cried in front of my ex.

20:35.275 --> 20:37.152
So I'm embarrassed. Happy now?

20:38.028 --> 20:39.529
Uh…

20:43.700 --> 20:46.328
[Ung] Like I said, for me running away
is not avoidance 

20:46.411 --> 20:47.746
but a reasonable decision.

20:50.916 --> 20:52.167
So sometimes…

20:53.335 --> 20:55.003
I don't make that decision.

20:57.464 --> 20:59.007
You wanna grab a bite?

21:01.635 --> 21:04.388
[alarm beeping]

21:05.222 --> 21:06.306
[soft chuckle]

21:08.141 --> 21:10.477
[soft music]

21:16.775 --> 21:19.069
EXCESSIVE LIFE
BEGINNING A JOURNEY

21:21.029 --> 21:22.239
[sighs]

21:25.534 --> 21:29.913
VOLUNTEER WITH NJ
BRIQUETTE DELIVERY OF LOVE

21:29.997 --> 21:31.999
[soft music]

21:33.959 --> 21:35.502
- Here.
- Thank you.

21:37.129 --> 21:37.963
[sighs]

21:38.046 --> 21:39.756
I don't know
what it is that you're thinking.

21:39.840 --> 21:42.467
[Chi-seong] If you don't wanna do this,
you can say no.

21:42.551 --> 21:43.593
It's volunteer work.

21:44.886 --> 21:46.722
You're not that warm-hearted, are you?

21:47.222 --> 21:48.932
[Chi-seong] This isn't helping you at all.

21:51.518 --> 21:54.146
Miss NJ, please have this.
I got it for you.

21:54.813 --> 21:56.148
You didn't have to, but thank you.

21:56.231 --> 21:59.151
Miss NJ, you look
more beautiful in person.

21:59.234 --> 22:01.069
Thank you very much.

22:01.153 --> 22:03.113
[girl chuckles]

22:05.991 --> 22:07.242
Where's your pride?

22:08.160 --> 22:12.039
VOLUNTEER WITH NJ
BRIQUETTE DELIVERY OF LOVE

22:12.122 --> 22:13.540
[girl] You all came here

22:13.623 --> 22:17.002
because NJ will drop the charges
if you do this, right?

22:17.085 --> 22:20.964
Yeah. I heard everyone who came
to do this were let off last year.

22:21.048 --> 22:22.966
That's right, she'll drop the charges.

22:23.050 --> 22:24.051
How do you know?

22:24.134 --> 22:27.346
Well, actually the truth is,
I came here last year too.

22:27.429 --> 22:28.805
Oh, gosh.

22:28.889 --> 22:30.682
Are you saying you got caught again?

22:30.766 --> 22:32.726
Well, I just had really bad luck.

22:32.809 --> 22:35.979
Honestly, they say everything
is a malicious comment these days.

22:36.063 --> 22:40.567
I guess so. To be honest,
don't you think this is ridiculous?

22:40.650 --> 22:43.570
Volunteer work with people
who wrote bad comments about her?

22:43.653 --> 22:46.990
I don't know if she has
really high self-esteem or if she's smart.

22:47.074 --> 22:49.201
It's all for her image, of course.

22:49.284 --> 22:50.619
She's a tough one, you know.

22:51.286 --> 22:54.206
Anyway, just keep sucking up to her
and she'll let you off.

22:54.289 --> 22:56.833
- Hang in there until it's over.
- [chuckles]

22:56.917 --> 23:00.337
By the way, did you see those stickers
on the lunch boxes?

23:00.420 --> 23:03.423
There's no way anyone here
would ever want to see her stupid face,

23:03.507 --> 23:05.300
- especially while they're eating.
- [chuckles]

23:05.383 --> 23:07.385
- I tore it off already.
- Oh.

23:07.469 --> 23:10.514
She's so young, but she's as sly as a fox.

23:10.597 --> 23:12.933
Hold on, what kind of comment
did you write?

23:13.016 --> 23:15.811
Oh, please. I didn't even
make up any stories about her.

23:16.394 --> 23:17.979
You know, there was something…

23:19.356 --> 23:22.901
there was a rumor
about NJ and her sponsors.

23:22.984 --> 23:24.820
And I just wrote about that a bit.

23:24.903 --> 23:27.739
[girl] Hold on, NJ even had sponsors?

23:27.823 --> 23:29.699
No way! Since when?

23:29.783 --> 23:30.951
[woman shushing]

23:31.034 --> 23:36.164
Her agency is willing going after
innocent citizens like us to keep quiet.

23:36.248 --> 23:37.415
[hater] I know, right?

23:37.499 --> 23:40.669
Remember when her first album
went viral right after her debut?

23:40.752 --> 23:44.172
I heard her sponsors got her
all those commercials back then.

23:44.256 --> 23:47.592
That's how she bought
all those expensive buildings at her age.

23:47.676 --> 23:48.969
[man] That's crazy.

23:49.594 --> 23:51.972
[somber music]

23:53.974 --> 23:56.184
[birds chirping]

24:00.856 --> 24:02.232
Come on. It's this way.

24:09.239 --> 24:10.657
WITH UNG

24:12.951 --> 24:15.579
Ung, what have you been doing all day?

24:16.246 --> 24:17.205
Good day to you.

24:19.207 --> 24:20.458
Oh, it's Yeon-su!

24:20.542 --> 24:21.668
[Ho] Yeon-su's here!

24:21.751 --> 24:25.505
[gasps]
Oh, my goodness! Yeon-su!

24:25.589 --> 24:28.800
Oh, I'm so glad you're here, Yeon-su.
[chuckles]

24:28.884 --> 24:30.552
- Are you here to eat?
- Yes.

24:31.219 --> 24:32.304
Oh. Sit over there.

24:33.096 --> 24:35.515
Were you able to get home safe last night?

24:35.599 --> 24:39.102
- Of course. Please have a seat here.
- [Ung] Can you even see me, Mom?

24:39.186 --> 24:40.103
[chuckles]

24:41.396 --> 24:43.148
- [Yeon-ok] It's been such a long time.
- Yes.

24:43.231 --> 24:45.650
What would you like, Yeon-su?
I'll cook anything for you.

24:45.734 --> 24:48.945
Oh, no. Anything is fine.
Everything you make is so delicious.

24:49.029 --> 24:52.324
But still. Is there anything
you're craving for?

24:52.407 --> 24:56.620
Well, do you still happen
to make that bean stew?

24:56.703 --> 24:59.998
Of course!
You used to love that, didn't you?

25:00.540 --> 25:01.917
I'll make some right away.

25:02.000 --> 25:03.710
- Thank you.
- Hey, Mom, I want--

25:03.793 --> 25:06.630
I'll get you some meat and some other
side dishes. Eat all you want, okay?

25:06.713 --> 25:08.465
- Thank you.
- [Chang-sik] Ho, I'm here.

25:09.132 --> 25:11.426
- Weren't you here just a minute ago?
- [chuckles]

25:12.677 --> 25:14.804
Oh. When did Ung get here?

25:14.888 --> 25:16.681
- Oh, hang on.
- [shushing]

25:16.765 --> 25:18.892
- Go.
- But, wait. Ji-ung…

25:19.476 --> 25:22.270
Ji-ung asked me to call him
if I ever saw Ung.

25:22.354 --> 25:25.023
All right. But don't call him, okay?
Just go away.

25:25.106 --> 25:26.900
[Chang-sik] Ji-ung was looking
everywhere for him.

25:27.484 --> 25:28.735
[Ho] Just go. Go!

25:30.195 --> 25:31.196
[inhales]

25:38.328 --> 25:40.413
Would looking through that
give you an answer?

25:40.497 --> 25:44.000
I'm pretty sure I told you
I don't like the smell of food in here.

25:44.084 --> 25:46.086
I'm done eating. You're so sensitive.

25:47.420 --> 25:48.421
[Dong-il] So did you eat?

25:49.256 --> 25:50.131
[Ji-ung] Yes, I ate.

25:51.132 --> 25:52.842
Outside the editing room.

25:54.302 --> 25:57.389
Hey, I heard they ran away.
[chuckles softly]

25:58.306 --> 26:02.060
You know, I'm surprised it took them
this long before they ran away.

26:02.894 --> 26:05.981
- They haven't changed a single bit, huh.
- You mean you knew?

26:06.690 --> 26:10.068
They ran away for about two weeks
when we filmed ten years ago.

26:10.151 --> 26:12.362
- [Dong-il] You didn't know?
- [deep inhale]

26:12.445 --> 26:14.614
The day Yeon-su went home,
and Ung was absent?

26:14.698 --> 26:16.032
That's right.

26:16.116 --> 26:18.994
They both disappeared without a word,
so we looked everywhere just to find them.

26:19.077 --> 26:21.705
- So where'd you end up finding them?
- We didn't find them.

26:22.330 --> 26:24.958
But they seemed to have
reached an agreement.

26:25.041 --> 26:27.377
They just returned
as if nothing happened at all.

26:27.877 --> 26:29.462
- What? Seriously?
- [Dong-il] It's obvious.

26:29.546 --> 26:31.798
They'll return
by themselves sooner or later,

26:31.881 --> 26:33.425
so just wait a bit before you swoop in.

26:33.508 --> 26:35.051
Don't worry about it so much.

26:35.969 --> 26:39.472
Hey, I hear Chae-ran was looking
for some lodging. Are you going somewhere?

26:39.556 --> 26:40.765
Can I join you guys?

26:40.849 --> 26:43.101
We are not going out to have fun.

26:43.184 --> 26:45.186
Ms. Lee wanted to come too,
but I turned her down.

26:45.270 --> 26:48.398
So don't even think about it.
Please grow up, the both of you.

26:49.774 --> 26:52.152
[indistinct chatter]

26:53.945 --> 26:57.032
I was able to compile a list
of places we can go to.

26:57.115 --> 26:59.034
Should we decide on one
after we find them?

26:59.117 --> 27:00.410
No, prepare it in advance.

27:00.493 --> 27:03.163
We won't have enough time afterward.
[inhales]

27:03.246 --> 27:06.833
In any case, I'll make sure
to get them today, no matter what.

27:10.462 --> 27:11.296
Is he useful?

27:11.379 --> 27:13.256
I told him to make a list of lodgings,

27:13.340 --> 27:17.052
and he gave me about 20 pages of places
where newlyweds would go.

27:17.135 --> 27:19.512
He's obviously good at organizing stuff.

27:19.596 --> 27:21.723
I already feel nauseous about it.

27:21.806 --> 27:23.016
He's so different from me.

27:24.768 --> 27:26.186
Mr. Kim!

27:26.269 --> 27:28.271
Going out on business?
I can drive you there, sir.

27:28.355 --> 27:29.647
No, it's fine.

27:30.565 --> 27:31.566
Oh, hey, Intern. You can--

27:31.649 --> 27:33.234
- You can--
- Im Tae-hun, that's my name.

27:33.318 --> 27:35.445
[scoffs]
Okay, Intern. Why don't you--

27:35.528 --> 27:37.155
Im Tae-hun, sir.
[chuckles]

27:38.406 --> 27:40.116
[quirky music sting]

27:41.576 --> 27:43.411
Okay, Imtern,
I'm calling you that from now on.

27:43.495 --> 27:46.623
Imtern, you go home.
Go and pack your things. Okay?

27:46.706 --> 27:48.041
Okay.

27:48.124 --> 27:49.918
- Chae-ran, wrap up here.
- Yes.

27:52.128 --> 27:53.797
- Imtern.
- Sir.

27:53.880 --> 27:56.257
[music fades]

28:15.026 --> 28:17.028
- Are you uncomfortable here?
- [groans]

28:18.029 --> 28:20.573
Uh, no, I was thinking
of visiting soon anyway.

28:21.533 --> 28:25.078
Uh, your parents seem
rather healthy today. I'm happy.

28:26.371 --> 28:29.290
Yeah. They have aged quite a lot, though.

28:31.000 --> 28:33.169
Your grandma? Is she doing all right?

28:33.837 --> 28:35.755
Mm-hm, she's good.

28:35.839 --> 28:37.257
- [cutlery clinking]
- Hm.

28:42.429 --> 28:44.681
- What are they saying?
- [Yeon-ok] I don't know.

28:44.764 --> 28:46.182
- Okay, give me that.
- Here.

28:46.266 --> 28:48.059
Wow, these radishes are really…

28:48.143 --> 28:49.936
You didn't answer my question yet.

28:53.565 --> 28:54.899
[whispers]
Come here.

28:58.278 --> 28:59.863
How have you been doing lately?

29:01.030 --> 29:02.198
[soft chuckle]

29:02.282 --> 29:05.452
Well, I, I just graduated and worked.

29:06.619 --> 29:07.537
Yeah.

29:08.455 --> 29:09.414
I did okay.

29:11.916 --> 29:12.792
Is that it?

29:13.626 --> 29:16.004
Mm-hm. It's nothing special.

29:17.756 --> 29:19.883
- Then yesterday was--
- Yesterday…

29:19.966 --> 29:21.801
I was just really drunk yesterday.

29:22.677 --> 29:25.054
[Yeon-su] It's embarrassing, so forget it.

29:25.138 --> 29:27.515
You know it was
because I was feeling stressed

29:27.599 --> 29:29.726
about this project that I was working on.

29:31.770 --> 29:34.314
[soft music]

29:37.484 --> 29:38.902
I enjoyed the food.

29:40.487 --> 29:41.529
I should get going.

29:42.906 --> 29:43.740
[Yeon-su groans]

29:44.657 --> 29:47.202
Wait, Yeon-su,
why are you leaving so soon?

29:47.285 --> 29:48.161
- Oh, gosh.
- Oh, uh,

29:48.244 --> 29:49.662
I really enjoyed the food you made.

29:49.746 --> 29:52.916
But I didn't expect to come here,
so I didn't bring anything.

29:52.999 --> 29:54.834
Oh, dear, there's no need for that.

29:54.918 --> 29:58.296
[Yeon-ok] You can come visit us
any time you like, all right?

29:58.379 --> 30:00.715
- [Yeon-su] Okay.
- [Yeon-ok] Oh, wait. Hang on.

30:00.799 --> 30:02.592
- I packed some side dishes for you.
- Wait here.

30:02.675 --> 30:04.385
- No, it's fine.
- No, no. Give them to her.

30:04.469 --> 30:06.262
[Yeon-ok] Here you go,
eat them with your grandmother.

30:07.138 --> 30:10.350
If you can, maybe next time
you can bring her along with you.

30:10.433 --> 30:11.976
There's really no need.
[inhales]

30:13.019 --> 30:15.522
But I'll be sure to enjoy these.
Thank you very much.

30:15.605 --> 30:16.731
- Come back again.
- Ung.

30:17.607 --> 30:19.734
- [Ho] Take her home.
- It's okay. I can go by myself.

30:19.818 --> 30:21.486
- No, no, no. Go on.
- Of course not!

30:22.904 --> 30:25.907
- [Ho] Come back soon, bye.
- [Yeon-su] Okay.

30:26.574 --> 30:27.992
You get home safely.

30:28.076 --> 30:29.202
[both chuckle]

30:29.953 --> 30:31.204
- Bye.
- [Yeon-su] Bye.

30:33.122 --> 30:35.708
[soft music]

30:38.336 --> 30:39.838
[Yeon-ok] How do they seem to you?

30:40.839 --> 30:42.882
Honestly, I don't have a single clue.

30:44.759 --> 30:46.177
[sighs deeply]

30:47.595 --> 30:49.889
[birds chirping]

30:51.891 --> 30:53.268
I used to say this to you,

30:53.351 --> 30:56.646
you should be good to your parents.
They're always so kind and nice.

30:59.816 --> 31:00.942
Are you going home?

31:01.776 --> 31:04.654
I don't suppose Ji-ung will still
be waiting there, will he?

31:05.989 --> 31:08.700
We both went AWOL
without telling any of them,

31:08.783 --> 31:10.827
so let's apologize
and start filming again…

31:11.578 --> 31:13.830
Right. It was this feeling.

31:15.623 --> 31:17.625
This is how I felt while dating you.

31:19.419 --> 31:21.212
I was like an idiot waiting for you,

31:22.213 --> 31:24.674
always watching you walk away,
step by step.

31:25.341 --> 31:26.467
That's how it was.

31:28.386 --> 31:30.305
What? What do you mean?

31:30.889 --> 31:33.391
Whenever you said you were okay,
I had to accept it.

31:34.893 --> 31:36.311
When you said nothing was wrong,

31:37.228 --> 31:39.063
I had to say I worried for no reason.

31:40.315 --> 31:41.816
When you wanted to break up,

31:42.775 --> 31:45.528
I had to accept without knowing why.

31:46.613 --> 31:48.573
And when I finally met you again,

31:49.866 --> 31:51.701
I had no idea how you'd be doing…

31:53.828 --> 31:56.414
or whatever it was that
you were thinking about at that time…

31:59.292 --> 32:02.712
but I had to just accept things.

32:02.795 --> 32:05.089
[Ung] "The best defense
is a good offense."

32:06.132 --> 32:08.635
It really feels like you're back, Yeon-su.
[sighs]

32:10.803 --> 32:12.055
Choi Ung.

32:12.138 --> 32:14.265
I'm really sick of this.

32:16.476 --> 32:18.519
[Ung] I guess I'm doing that right now.

32:21.898 --> 32:25.234
But this was not my choice at all.

32:28.071 --> 32:30.615
["Maybe If" by BIBI playing]

32:47.173 --> 32:49.509
- [photographer] One, two, three!
- [camera shutter clicks]

32:50.426 --> 32:51.594
[all] Good job.

32:51.678 --> 32:53.262
- Good job!
- [all cheer]

32:53.930 --> 32:55.848
- Good job.
- [all] Good job, everyone.

32:55.932 --> 32:57.350
Miss NJ.

32:58.393 --> 33:01.646
Thanks to you, I, uh, had
a really meaningful experience today.

33:01.729 --> 33:02.855
[man] Thank you.

33:04.023 --> 33:08.277
Thanks to today, we were able
to reflect on ourselves and our actions.

33:08.361 --> 33:11.239
Thank you so much
for giving us this opportunity.

33:11.322 --> 33:13.449
This means
you're going to let us off, right?

33:13.533 --> 33:14.784
[girl] Jeez.

33:15.618 --> 33:18.830
We promise that we will do our best
to make up for our mistakes.

33:18.913 --> 33:22.959
And also, we'll tell everyone
we know about how cool you were today.

33:23.042 --> 33:24.627
- Okay?
- [laughter]

33:24.711 --> 33:25.670
[chuckles]

33:26.921 --> 33:29.132
Sure. All right.

33:30.174 --> 33:31.342
[laughs]

33:32.385 --> 33:34.220
- Hey, Director.
- [director] Yes?

33:34.303 --> 33:37.056
[NJ] I'm sorry,
but I can't come here anymore.

33:37.140 --> 33:37.974
And why not?

33:38.057 --> 33:40.143
I thought they would end
after a few times.

33:40.226 --> 33:42.812
I didn't think there would be
an endless line of trolls.

33:44.605 --> 33:45.773
They're not my fans at all.

33:46.941 --> 33:48.943
They're the internet trolls I sued.

33:49.027 --> 33:50.611
- Hey, NJ.
- What?

33:50.695 --> 33:52.280
Who? Me?

33:52.989 --> 33:56.784
Oh, well, you always seemed
to call me a bitch, didn't you?

33:56.868 --> 33:58.786
- [dramatic music]
- [sighs]

33:59.537 --> 34:02.165
- I'm not dropping the charges.
- [shocked whispers]

34:02.248 --> 34:03.583
Good work today, everyone.

34:04.459 --> 34:06.586
Thank you for joining me
when I asked you all

34:06.669 --> 34:08.463
if you wanted to do some volunteer work.

34:08.546 --> 34:10.006
[NJ] Get home safely.

34:10.089 --> 34:12.508
- But…
- Wait a second. You can't just do this!

34:12.592 --> 34:15.553
It's not fair. This is such a scam.

34:16.220 --> 34:19.849
You said you'd drop the charges
against us. This is so ridiculous.

34:22.518 --> 34:26.397
Did I? I don't think
I ever promised to drop the charges.

34:26.481 --> 34:27.732
[scoffs]

34:27.815 --> 34:29.942
You ate with me here last year, right?

34:30.026 --> 34:32.236
Did you troll me
because you wanted to see me again?

34:32.320 --> 34:33.780
Well, that was…

34:35.198 --> 34:38.159
Can't I even criticize you?
Is it all trolling to you?

34:38.242 --> 34:39.535
- [soft chuckle]
- [rasps]

34:41.037 --> 34:44.624
Should I read the comments
you wrote about me to everyone here then?

34:45.458 --> 34:48.002
Let's see if it's criticism
or just trolling.

34:48.086 --> 34:49.378
- Hey, wait.
- What?

34:49.462 --> 34:52.882
You're just abusing the power you have
against the innocent citizens.

34:52.965 --> 34:54.425
We're all busy people, you know.

34:54.509 --> 34:56.636
You were just making us
waste our time here!

34:57.720 --> 35:00.306
You'd better suck up to me
if you at least want a lower sentence.

35:01.599 --> 35:02.725
Are you sure about this?

35:02.809 --> 35:04.769
[tense music]

35:05.478 --> 35:07.897
[shocked whispers]

35:08.689 --> 35:09.690
Miss NJ.

35:10.191 --> 35:14.112
As you know, uh,
I only made this mistake once.

35:14.695 --> 35:18.533
If I get charged for this,
I'll have a hard time getting a job.

35:18.616 --> 35:22.203
My life is at stake here.
Can you please let me off this time?

35:22.286 --> 35:24.455
[tense music continues]

35:24.539 --> 35:25.706
[soft chuckle]

35:25.790 --> 35:28.835
All right. After all,
you only did it once, right?

35:28.918 --> 35:30.128
[relieved sigh]

35:30.211 --> 35:31.754
So I'll only sue you just once.

35:32.547 --> 35:34.715
And if you do it twice,
then I'll sue you twice.

35:35.883 --> 35:40.263
[nervous chuckle]
Hey, people can make mistakes sometimes.

35:40.346 --> 35:41.848
Do you have to be so cruel
because of that?

35:41.931 --> 35:45.434
How can you write sexually harassing
comments with such detail by mistake?

35:45.518 --> 35:47.103
Your ID is Bibibik, right?

35:47.895 --> 35:49.856
VOLUNTEER WITH NJ
BRIQUETTE DELIVERY OF LOVE

35:51.023 --> 35:53.234
There were articles
about how this was a place

35:53.317 --> 35:55.153
for reconciliation and forgiveness.

35:55.236 --> 35:57.196
[NJ] Go and tell people that it isn't.

35:57.280 --> 36:00.116
Go ahead and tell everyone
that I'm just a crazy bitch

36:00.199 --> 36:01.742
who was bent on suing you.

36:01.826 --> 36:04.120
And I was acting unlike myself.

36:06.205 --> 36:07.415
Tell them all…

36:08.749 --> 36:10.042
like you always do.

36:11.586 --> 36:14.005
[haters clamoring in protest]

36:15.631 --> 36:17.175
Can't believe her.

36:17.258 --> 36:18.467
[music fades]

36:18.551 --> 36:20.636
[birds chirping]

36:23.222 --> 36:24.640
[groans]
Damn it.

36:25.975 --> 36:27.518
Why did I say that?

36:27.602 --> 36:31.647
[Ung] I just wanted to go back home
and sleep all day.

36:33.441 --> 36:34.567
[phone buzzing]

36:37.653 --> 36:39.030
WHY DID YOU TWO SUDDENLY GO AWOL?

36:41.657 --> 36:43.826
- [Sol-i] Choi Ung!
- [Eun-ho] Choi Ung!

36:43.910 --> 36:45.786
Congratulations!

36:45.870 --> 36:48.080
We know that you're far away right now,

36:48.164 --> 36:49.999
but we're still congratulating you.

36:50.082 --> 36:51.667
- Super punch!
- [laughs]

36:51.751 --> 36:54.212
You said you liked
how happy you are in this picture.

36:54.295 --> 36:57.340
Right? You're happy, aren't you?
Why don't you smile, huh?

36:57.423 --> 37:00.509
Hey, I heard you're earning a fortune.

37:00.593 --> 37:03.137
Maybe you can buy my bar? Please, Ung?

37:03.221 --> 37:06.974
Ung, you and I have finally succeeded.

37:07.058 --> 37:11.145
I can't believe that the dim-witted Ung
has succeeded this much.

37:11.229 --> 37:12.563
I'm so proud of you!

37:12.647 --> 37:14.190
[quivers]
I just feel so…

37:14.941 --> 37:18.277
I… I still can't believe… I…

37:18.361 --> 37:22.031
got to see my idiot friend succeed…

37:22.114 --> 37:25.201
Oh, no, I'm going to start crying too!

37:25.284 --> 37:27.662
[Eun-ho] He didn't even
get to eat properly…

37:27.745 --> 37:29.288
- Oh! Don't cry.
- [sobs]

37:29.372 --> 37:32.333
He suffered so much, you know that?

37:32.416 --> 37:33.417
Hey!

37:33.918 --> 37:37.922
You have to be happy, you understand?
You got that, huh?

37:39.715 --> 37:40.549
[sighs]

37:40.633 --> 37:43.177
It looks more
like they're holding my funeral.

37:44.804 --> 37:46.180
Should I report them?

37:47.098 --> 37:49.225
- Eun-ho's an ass.
- [phone buzzes]

37:49.308 --> 37:50.559
Huh?

37:50.643 --> 37:52.270
NJ

37:52.353 --> 37:53.771
[buzzing continues]

37:59.485 --> 38:00.778
[Ung] It was this feeling.

38:01.445 --> 38:03.572
I was like an idiot waiting for you,

38:03.656 --> 38:06.367
always watching you walk away,
step by step.

38:07.076 --> 38:08.244
That's how it was.

38:09.161 --> 38:11.163
I'm really sick of this.

38:11.247 --> 38:12.456
[Ja-gyeong] Yeon-su?

38:13.165 --> 38:14.959
[somber music]

38:17.336 --> 38:19.839
Hey, why are you standing there?

38:19.922 --> 38:22.133
- Did you just get here?
- Oh.

38:23.301 --> 38:25.094
What's that in your hand?

38:30.725 --> 38:32.977
Uh, Grandma, I'll be back
in a moment, okay?

38:33.060 --> 38:34.979
- Wait, didn't you just get home?
- [door opens]

38:35.563 --> 38:36.647
[door closes]

38:37.815 --> 38:40.109
[Chi-seong] You should have
just done that a long time ago.

38:40.192 --> 38:41.986
It's not something you can forgive easily.

38:42.069 --> 38:44.947
"The angelic NJ
who forgives her online haters"?

38:45.031 --> 38:46.365
To hell with that nonsense.

38:46.449 --> 38:49.910
Tell our agency that you won't be
dropping charges for anyone anymore.

38:50.745 --> 38:52.288
What a bunch of jerks.

38:53.372 --> 38:54.457
Hey…

38:55.333 --> 38:56.375
what's gotten into you?

38:56.459 --> 38:58.544
Why did you wanna
meet them in person anyway?

38:59.337 --> 39:00.504
I thought…

39:02.048 --> 39:04.925
it'd be less scary
if I saw the real people behind it all.

39:06.427 --> 39:08.763
Just avoid them. Run away.

39:09.930 --> 39:11.098
It's okay.

39:14.518 --> 39:16.562
[wind gusting]

39:19.357 --> 39:21.317
That's why I'm running away this time.

39:23.402 --> 39:24.779
Where? To that guy again?

39:26.364 --> 39:28.449
[light music]

39:28.532 --> 39:29.784
[chuckles]

39:29.867 --> 39:30.868
Yes.

39:33.537 --> 39:34.830
Choi Ung!

39:35.998 --> 39:37.166
[gasps]
Oh.

39:37.666 --> 39:39.168
- [chuckles]
- Oh.

39:40.211 --> 39:43.297
- Oh…
- [chuckles]

39:43.881 --> 39:45.841
[NJ] I guess I called at the perfect time.

39:46.801 --> 39:49.887
Tell me, were you wandering around
after running away from home?

39:49.970 --> 39:51.972
Please, running away at this age?

39:52.056 --> 39:53.349
I was…
[inhales]

39:54.058 --> 39:56.519
…just trying to have some time
for myself, that's all.

39:56.602 --> 39:59.105
If you don't want
to do the documentary, don't.

39:59.188 --> 40:03.067
It'd be quite overwhelming for someone
who isn't a celebrity.

40:06.070 --> 40:07.363
[sighs]

40:08.155 --> 40:09.156
[gasps]

40:13.369 --> 40:14.912
It's okay. Come here.

40:15.413 --> 40:17.373
You can bring those bags too.

40:17.957 --> 40:20.376
[light music]

40:23.671 --> 40:26.841
Wow, no way! NJ?

40:26.924 --> 40:29.051
You're the NJ? Really?

40:29.135 --> 40:31.095
Mm-hm. Do you have a pen?

40:31.178 --> 40:32.179
Oh.

40:32.263 --> 40:34.014
[rustles]

40:35.224 --> 40:37.726
[light music continues]

40:39.353 --> 40:43.566
Hey, kid. You should ask permission first
before taking photos of someone.

40:43.649 --> 40:44.900
Can I please take a photo?

40:44.984 --> 40:46.360
No, you can't.

40:46.444 --> 40:49.155
[NJ] There are lots
of pretty photos online.

40:49.864 --> 40:51.031
- Wow.
- Here.

40:51.657 --> 40:53.784
Do you kids know what scarcity is?

40:54.577 --> 40:55.619
What about rare items?

40:55.703 --> 40:57.121
- Yes.
- Yes.

40:57.830 --> 41:00.332
If you want your bags
to become rare items,

41:00.416 --> 41:04.378
you shouldn't tell anyone that I was here
or that you saw me here. You got that?

41:05.045 --> 41:06.255
- Okay.
- Okay.

41:06.338 --> 41:08.132
If you tell people I'm here,

41:08.215 --> 41:11.010
I'll end up signing
every single person's bags.

41:11.844 --> 41:13.721
- So you shouldn't?
- [both] Yes.

41:13.804 --> 41:15.848
Run along now. I'm talking to my friend.

41:16.432 --> 41:18.058
- Thank you very much.
- Thank you very much.

41:19.518 --> 41:21.103
[kids chuckling]

41:21.187 --> 41:22.438
[gasps]

41:23.105 --> 41:25.649
Even little kids recognize you, huh?

41:26.233 --> 41:27.651
It must be tiring, though.

41:28.569 --> 41:31.238
Regular citizens like you
don't know what it's like.

41:32.448 --> 41:35.826
Wait. I think you should understand
a bit about it by now.

41:37.286 --> 41:40.122
Well, there were some who did recognize me

41:40.206 --> 41:42.625
only because of that stupid documentary.

41:42.708 --> 41:44.627
Then why are you filming it again?

41:45.419 --> 41:47.254
I don't know. It just sort of happened.

41:47.755 --> 41:50.674
I've fallen into my own trap, I guess.

41:50.758 --> 41:53.594
Well, that happens sometimes.

41:58.140 --> 41:59.141
[Ung sighs]

42:00.518 --> 42:01.936
[laughs]

42:04.104 --> 42:05.940
Did you really just laugh at me?

42:06.941 --> 42:08.943
Let's eat lunch together.

42:09.026 --> 42:11.987
Oh, sorry but I just ate.

42:12.655 --> 42:15.074
[chuckling]

42:15.157 --> 42:20.037
Mr. Choi. I really didn't want to say
this sort of thing to you myself, but…

42:20.579 --> 42:22.248
I'm actually a type A.

42:22.331 --> 42:24.959
My Myers Briggs is actually ISFP,

42:25.042 --> 42:28.003
so I'm introverted and sensitive
even though I don't seem like it.

42:28.087 --> 42:30.714
That's why I wrote some things down
in my heart diary earlier.

42:31.632 --> 42:32.925
A what diary?

42:33.008 --> 42:33.884
First of all.

42:34.510 --> 42:36.971
"Mr. Choi got famous
because I bought one of his works,

42:37.054 --> 42:39.598
but why doesn't he want to buy me a meal?"

42:39.682 --> 42:40.724
[NJ] Secondly.

42:40.808 --> 42:42.351
"I asked him to draw my buildings,

42:42.434 --> 42:45.145
but why is that he doesn't want
to contact me even one?"

42:45.896 --> 42:47.356
- [inhales]
- And thirdly.

42:47.439 --> 42:49.108
"I made him even more popular

42:49.191 --> 42:52.361
by going to his drawing show
when I wasn't even invited,

42:52.444 --> 42:55.406
but why hasn't he asked me out
still until now?"

42:55.489 --> 42:56.448
Well, I--

42:56.532 --> 42:59.243
Those are the three debts that
you have with me right now.

42:59.326 --> 43:00.869
So how will you pay me that?

43:01.996 --> 43:03.998
[light awkward music]

43:04.999 --> 43:05.833
[sighs]

43:05.916 --> 43:07.167
[chuckles]

43:11.422 --> 43:12.506
[sighs]

43:13.465 --> 43:16.719
Does he think he's the only one
who can get upset? Unbelievable.

43:17.303 --> 43:19.680
[scoffs]
When did he ever tell me anything anyway?

43:19.763 --> 43:22.808
Choi Ung was always the one who hid…
[Yeon-su groans]

43:22.891 --> 43:24.935
Why the hell isn't he picking up?

43:25.019 --> 43:26.729
…whenever he was upset.

43:26.812 --> 43:28.063
[chimes]

43:28.147 --> 43:29.607
[line trilling]

43:32.901 --> 43:36.113
Oh, I think…

43:38.282 --> 43:41.118
This is something that I didn't expect.

43:42.578 --> 43:43.704
Yeon-su.

43:47.958 --> 43:48.959
Uh…

43:50.419 --> 43:51.295
Oh.

43:52.338 --> 43:56.216
[NJ] Seriously,
why are you always so clumsy?

43:56.300 --> 43:57.509
[chuckles]

43:57.593 --> 44:00.804
Anyway, I thought everyone
would pretend not to have eaten

44:00.888 --> 44:02.723
if I asked to have a meal together.

44:03.223 --> 44:04.933
You're so difficult to deal with.

44:05.017 --> 44:06.560
[deep inhale]

44:06.644 --> 44:08.937
Uh, well, NJ, um…

44:09.021 --> 44:12.650
I notice that you always gotten
in touch with me like this.

44:13.359 --> 44:15.319
And you just keep on popping up.

44:17.112 --> 44:20.074
I've been pretty clueless, haven't I?

44:22.076 --> 44:25.204
But weren't you pretending to be clueless?

44:25.287 --> 44:26.872
Oh, I guess that's true…

44:28.999 --> 44:31.377
I'm sorry. I guess
I should have mentioned it first.

44:31.460 --> 44:33.003
My point, exactly.

44:33.712 --> 44:36.048
It's way too embarrassing
for me to say it myself.

44:38.008 --> 44:39.093
Well…

44:42.763 --> 44:45.349
Since you bought three drawings,
I'll give you one for free.

44:45.432 --> 44:47.935
Look, I don't usually do this,
but I'll make an exception

44:48.018 --> 44:50.771
- since you're NJ, if there's anything--
- Hold on a minute, Mr. Choi.

44:50.854 --> 44:52.398
I have a lot of money.

44:52.481 --> 44:55.734
Do you think really I'm doing this
just to get a free drawing?

44:56.360 --> 44:59.696
Huh? Then why are you being so nice to me?

45:00.739 --> 45:02.783
- Do I need a reason?
- [gasps]

45:02.866 --> 45:04.868
[stammers]
No, that's not what I mean.

45:04.952 --> 45:07.371
- I meant that I don't get why you would--
- Because I like you.

45:07.454 --> 45:08.330
Huh?

45:09.206 --> 45:10.999
- Oh!
- [gasps]

45:11.083 --> 45:14.169
Oh, no, why do you make such a mess?

45:15.087 --> 45:16.296
What do…

45:16.380 --> 45:18.090
[chuckles]

45:18.173 --> 45:20.759
I just had a really tough day today.

45:21.385 --> 45:25.139
I didn't want to whine about it to you
because it's a pretty normal thing for me.

45:26.473 --> 45:27.808
But then…

45:28.392 --> 45:30.686
[NJ] I always feel better
whenever I see you.

45:31.687 --> 45:34.064
At first, I felt better
when I saw your drawings.

45:34.815 --> 45:36.775
But now, I feel it with you too.

45:37.943 --> 45:41.071
And that is my reason
for coming to see you.

45:42.072 --> 45:44.491
So stop getting so startled
whenever you see me.

45:45.159 --> 45:46.702
And don't always look so shocked either.

45:47.619 --> 45:50.998
I'm not saying I love you, nor that
it means that I'm asking you out.

45:51.081 --> 45:54.084
All I'm saying is that I like you.
[inhales]

45:54.168 --> 45:57.796
Maybe it's because
you kind of look like my Tofu.

45:59.465 --> 46:00.716
"Tofu"?

46:00.799 --> 46:02.384
Mm. My pet dog.

46:03.677 --> 46:04.845
Oh, your dog.

46:04.928 --> 46:07.097
[light music]

46:09.099 --> 46:10.893
Are you going somewhere?

46:10.976 --> 46:13.687
Sometimes there are kids
who just don't listen.

46:14.563 --> 46:16.648
I should get going.
Let's hang out again some time.

46:17.524 --> 46:19.359
You should go home too while you can.

46:20.402 --> 46:22.237
[kids shouting excitedly]

46:26.867 --> 46:29.203
- They're back again.
- [kids shouting excitedly]

46:31.455 --> 46:33.540
[light music continues]

46:35.626 --> 46:36.793
[sighs]

46:37.669 --> 46:39.254
You're so unbelievable.

46:39.338 --> 46:40.964
Were you looking for me all day?

46:41.048 --> 46:43.550
No, I just started looking for you.

46:43.634 --> 46:45.719
And I just so happened
to get lucky and bump into you.

46:45.802 --> 46:47.429
I didn't even have to go very far.

46:48.263 --> 46:50.724
- So what were you doing?
- Oh, walking.

46:50.807 --> 46:52.059
[Yeon-su clears throat]

46:59.650 --> 47:00.526
Okay.

47:01.193 --> 47:02.903
Then why did you run away today?

47:03.904 --> 47:05.155
I just needed a break.

47:05.864 --> 47:07.032
You just needed a break?

47:07.115 --> 47:10.911
Mm, yeah. I just wanted to feel
some freedom today. That's all.

47:10.994 --> 47:14.081
Is that so? You should have told me then.
You'll be free from us very soon.

47:14.164 --> 47:16.250
- What?
- Nothing. Never mind that.

47:17.376 --> 47:19.002
Are you still gonna be in it?

47:21.463 --> 47:23.465
I'm just confirming. Don't answer that.

47:23.549 --> 47:24.633
- Hey.
- Sorry.

47:28.762 --> 47:30.222
Did you fight with Ung again?

47:30.305 --> 47:34.142
No, not really.
He just got angry with me. That's all.

47:34.226 --> 47:36.562
When on earth did he become
so short-tempered?

47:37.271 --> 47:38.438
When do you think?

47:40.399 --> 47:42.818
[clears throat, sighs]

47:42.901 --> 47:44.736
Fine. Everything's my fault.

47:44.820 --> 47:47.990
Well, I wouldn't say everything.
Maybe about half.

47:48.073 --> 47:49.866
It's around half and half with Ung.

47:49.950 --> 47:50.951
It's half?

47:51.702 --> 47:54.746
Breaking up isn't usually
just one person's fault.

47:54.830 --> 47:56.206
It's the same for both sides.

48:01.920 --> 48:04.089
- What is it? Something wrong?
- [deep inhale]

48:04.172 --> 48:06.341
You seem to know a lot about dating.

48:07.426 --> 48:08.468
What?

48:08.552 --> 48:10.470
Tell me, are you seeing someone?

48:11.847 --> 48:13.307
[chuckles]
Gosh.

48:14.433 --> 48:16.018
[chuckles]
Guess you're not.

48:16.101 --> 48:17.394
Have you ever dated before?

48:17.477 --> 48:20.772
Yeon-su. You see, there are
two kinds of men in this world.

48:20.856 --> 48:22.774
Men who can't date,
and men who don't date.

48:22.858 --> 48:24.610
So you're a guy who can't date.

48:24.693 --> 48:26.361
[laughs]

48:27.154 --> 48:28.363
What? You're so ridiculous.

48:28.447 --> 48:31.742
I think that you'd be shocked to find out
just the kind of person I really am.

48:31.825 --> 48:33.619
Really? What kind of person are you?

48:34.995 --> 48:36.955
Well, I'm the bad boy type.

48:38.498 --> 48:40.083
You know what a homme fatale is, right?

48:40.167 --> 48:43.587
The "fatale" means the attraction
could be fatal to women. That's me.

48:43.670 --> 48:47.007
That's why I try to keep my attractiveness
hidden so I won't harm others.

48:47.090 --> 48:49.092
[inhales]
Oh, Kim Ji-ung.

48:49.176 --> 48:51.553
When did you become so shameless, huh?

48:52.262 --> 48:53.639
You're so funny.

48:54.890 --> 48:56.975
That wasn't a joke, you know. I'm serious.

48:57.059 --> 49:01.104
Yeah, but you were a bit popular
when we were in high school, remember?

49:01.188 --> 49:02.314
[sighs]
You finally get me.

49:02.397 --> 49:03.398
But why, though?

49:04.232 --> 49:06.109
Hey, that's kind of mean, you know.

49:06.193 --> 49:08.695
I guess it helped that
you were the student president.

49:09.696 --> 49:11.573
You just didn't know me much back then.

49:11.657 --> 49:13.784
[light music]

49:16.620 --> 49:18.246
[Sol-i] I'm getting drunk.

49:20.832 --> 49:22.334
[Yeon-su] That idiot.

49:23.168 --> 49:25.504
- Is that Sol-i?
- [deep sigh]

49:25.587 --> 49:27.798
She's the finale of my terrible day.

49:28.632 --> 49:29.675
[Yeon-su] Sol-i!

49:29.758 --> 49:31.259
- [Ji-ung] Sol-i.
- [Sol-i groans]

49:31.343 --> 49:32.511
[Yeon-su] Sol-i!

49:33.428 --> 49:34.930
Kook Yeon-su!

49:35.806 --> 49:38.850
[singing]
♪ You're my heartbreaker ♪

49:38.934 --> 49:40.102
[Yeon-su] What's all this?

49:40.185 --> 49:42.020
- I'm drunk.
- Wow.

49:44.272 --> 49:45.565
[gasps]

49:45.649 --> 49:49.111
[gasping, grunting]

49:52.948 --> 49:54.032
Eun-ho?

49:56.660 --> 49:58.912
[cheeky music]

50:04.251 --> 50:06.211
Are you finally dead?

50:08.547 --> 50:10.132
[snoring softly]

50:11.508 --> 50:12.759
[sighs]

50:12.843 --> 50:15.095
[cheeky music continues]

50:19.516 --> 50:21.226
I know this isn't a raise,

50:21.309 --> 50:23.645
but you're better off gone
than getting one.

50:24.938 --> 50:25.981
[Eun-ho groaning]

50:26.064 --> 50:28.275
You made a total mess in here.

50:30.026 --> 50:32.070
- [sighs]
- [Sol-i] I'm going to puke.

50:33.071 --> 50:35.991
- You're so unbelievable.
- [Sol-i] Oh, I'm going to puke.

50:36.908 --> 50:38.994
- [groans]
- You're such a pain, you know?

50:39.077 --> 50:40.162
[squeals]

50:41.288 --> 50:43.039
Is it really okay for her
to sleep in here?

50:43.123 --> 50:44.291
Her dad's a minister.

50:44.374 --> 50:46.710
Believe it or not,
her family's very religious.

50:46.793 --> 50:48.378
They don't know that she actually drinks.

50:48.462 --> 50:49.838
I love you, God.

50:50.672 --> 50:53.008
How do they not know
that she's running a bar?

50:53.091 --> 50:54.926
Well, you should really see
her act some time.

50:55.010 --> 50:57.387
She should have been an actress,
not a writer.

50:58.180 --> 51:01.099
- I love you, sachangnim.
- No, go to sleep.

51:01.183 --> 51:03.560
I'm sorry you got dragged into this.

51:04.060 --> 51:06.938
- What's going on here?
- [Ji-ung] Grandma!

51:07.022 --> 51:10.859
Oh, good Lord. Aren't you Ji-ung? Oh, my.

51:10.942 --> 51:13.445
- It's so nice to see you.
- How have you been?

51:13.528 --> 51:15.197
It looks like you got so much younger.

51:15.280 --> 51:17.115
- Oh, come on.
- [both chuckle]

51:17.199 --> 51:18.158
- How are you?
- Hold it.

51:18.241 --> 51:19.868
Since when were you two so close, huh?

51:19.951 --> 51:23.497
Oh, don't you know?
Ji-ung's the sweetest boy I've ever met.

51:24.581 --> 51:25.707
Have you eaten, Ung?

51:25.791 --> 51:27.751
- How about something to eat, huh?
- All right.

51:27.834 --> 51:30.629
[sniffs air]
What the hell is that stench?

51:31.213 --> 51:33.173
[singing]
♪ It's me, it's me ♪

51:33.256 --> 51:35.675
Oh, that little brat!
Is that troublemaker drunk again?

51:35.759 --> 51:37.219
- Please, can you leave my room now?
- Where did you go

51:37.302 --> 51:38.345
- to get plastered like that?
- Go on. Go.

51:38.428 --> 51:40.555
- Oh, goodness this girl.
- [Ji-ung chuckles]

51:43.767 --> 51:45.393
Welcome!

51:53.276 --> 51:54.861
[plastic rustles]

51:59.366 --> 52:02.285
[Eun-ho] Ung! My Ung who ran away.

52:02.786 --> 52:05.288
I knew you'd be successful one day.

52:05.997 --> 52:08.667
- I'm so proud of what you've become.
- [appreciative chuckle]

52:09.543 --> 52:11.711
I'm still not forgiving you.
[clicks tongue]

52:12.629 --> 52:14.214
[Eun-ho] Continued at the back.

52:15.465 --> 52:18.468
You may be a sore loser
who failed hard at love,

52:19.052 --> 52:22.389
but you succeeded in your career.
Let's work hard!

52:22.472 --> 52:26.184
- [scoffs]
- [Sol-i] It's me, Sol-i.

52:26.268 --> 52:28.436
- Can you give me 20 million won please?
- [chuckles]

52:29.104 --> 52:30.647
- [Ung] Jackass!
- [Eun-ho] Ow!

52:31.314 --> 52:32.983
[Eun-ho] Why did you kick me?

52:34.651 --> 52:35.986
[sighs deeply]

52:38.530 --> 52:41.199
[soft gentle music]

52:41.908 --> 52:43.076
[groans]

52:45.829 --> 52:47.122
Here you go.

52:47.205 --> 52:50.375
My dear, what have you
been doing these days?

52:50.458 --> 52:53.295
- [Ji-ung] I'm filming Ung and Yeon-su.
- The documentary?

52:53.378 --> 52:56.506
- [Ji-ung] Yes.
- Oh, my! Will it be on TV, then?

52:56.590 --> 52:58.466
- [Ji-ung] Yes, of course.
- [Ja-gyeong laughs]

52:58.550 --> 52:59.843
[Ja-gyeong] You boy.

53:02.137 --> 53:04.139
[soft gentle music]

53:06.850 --> 53:07.934
[sighs]

53:11.062 --> 53:12.230
[groans]

53:16.151 --> 53:17.694
Why are you so early?

53:17.777 --> 53:19.279
Come. Let's take a ride.

53:20.030 --> 53:21.239
Are you half-asleep?

53:21.323 --> 53:23.366
You said you wanted
to feel some freedom, right?

53:23.992 --> 53:27.370
- Let's go get some fresh air.
- No, I wanna stay home.

53:29.331 --> 53:30.498
- [honks horn]
- Hey!

53:31.333 --> 53:34.586
What are you doing? Are you trying
to wake the whole neighborhood?

53:34.669 --> 53:37.631
- Well, why shouldn't I?
- Cut if off! Don't do that!

53:37.714 --> 53:38.882
Just get in.

53:38.965 --> 53:40.508
[annoyed sigh]

53:44.638 --> 53:46.431
[Ung] In American horror films,

53:46.514 --> 53:50.101
crimes usually happen
suddenly in broad daylight.

53:54.105 --> 53:55.774
- [groans]
- Going somewhere?

54:02.948 --> 54:04.157
Where are you going?

54:08.745 --> 54:09.996
What?

54:11.665 --> 54:13.875
[suspenseful music]

54:15.543 --> 54:20.173
When the victim is at his most vulnerable,
that's when they attack.

54:23.760 --> 54:25.804
[suspenseful music rises]

54:29.474 --> 54:31.559
[engine revs]

54:34.437 --> 54:36.231
And the criminal is usually…

54:37.774 --> 54:39.442
someone close to him.

54:44.155 --> 54:45.407
[grunts]

54:46.032 --> 54:47.367
What are you doing?

54:54.207 --> 54:56.876
[bright expectant music]

55:07.762 --> 55:10.056
[bright music continues]

55:16.646 --> 55:18.148
[engine stops]

55:21.985 --> 55:24.154
[groans]
Choi Ung's guerilla gig!

55:24.237 --> 55:26.031
I wonder how many fans will be here today?

55:26.614 --> 55:29.367
- [Eun-ho] All right. Get out. Get out!
- [Ung struggling]

55:29.451 --> 55:30.910
Come on, enjoy the view.

55:31.494 --> 55:33.204
What do you think you're doing?

55:33.288 --> 55:36.583
You didn't say a single word
during the whole four-hour drive!

55:36.666 --> 55:37.667
What…

55:38.376 --> 55:40.920
Hey! Where's your boss right now, huh?
I'm going to sue…

55:41.713 --> 55:43.506
[engine revs]

55:48.678 --> 55:50.972
- Hey, Kim Ji-ung!
- Move!

55:52.098 --> 55:53.391
[Ji-ung] You got here safe.

55:53.475 --> 55:56.770
Hey, Kim Ji-ung. This prank
is neither fun, nor impressive, okay.

55:56.853 --> 56:00.148
I have no idea
what you're trying to do here, but…

56:00.231 --> 56:02.609
[soft twinkling music]

56:06.029 --> 56:09.532
[Ung] So the genre of this
isn't really romance…

56:11.534 --> 56:14.788
Well, guess we're all here now.
We'll be staying here for three days.

56:15.997 --> 56:17.624
[Eun-ho] Wow, we have seven fans today!

56:17.707 --> 56:19.793
- [Ung] …it's actually horror.
- [Eun-ho] Round of applause!

56:21.294 --> 56:24.130
I'm sure you've noticed,
but you can't leave without a car.

56:24.798 --> 56:27.258
[Ji-ung] If you wanna go home,
you'll have to walk all the way.

56:27.967 --> 56:29.302
It will take you days, though.

56:29.385 --> 56:30.845
Hey, Kim Ji-ung!

56:32.180 --> 56:34.849
[tense music]

56:34.933 --> 56:37.060
[Ung] A cliche horror-thriller film…

56:37.727 --> 56:39.062
that always releases…

56:39.771 --> 56:41.272
at this time of year.

56:41.356 --> 56:43.483
[tense music rises]

56:47.695 --> 56:49.322
EPILOGUE

56:49.405 --> 56:50.532
- [cameraman] Hey, sir.
- Hmm.

56:50.615 --> 56:52.033
[cameraman] Choi Ung isn't here today.

56:53.493 --> 56:55.411
- What? He's not here?
- [cameraman] No.

56:57.539 --> 57:00.750
[Dong-il gasps]
No wonder he wasn't picking up earlier.

57:00.834 --> 57:03.253
[indistinct chatter]

57:10.009 --> 57:11.261
Uh, excuse me, sir.

57:12.178 --> 57:13.179
[gasps]
Yes?

57:14.097 --> 57:16.683
Will it be okay for me
to leave school early?

57:16.766 --> 57:18.226
Why? Are you feeling sick?

57:20.061 --> 57:20.979
Yes.

57:21.062 --> 57:23.857
[teacher] Right. You must be overworked
with studying and filming lately.

57:23.940 --> 57:25.400
Sure. Go and get some rest.

57:28.486 --> 57:30.572
[indistinct chatter]

57:32.031 --> 57:33.283
NO LONGER HUMAN
CHEKHOV SHORT STORIES

57:43.960 --> 57:44.794
Hi.

57:48.465 --> 57:49.966
Why are you here?

57:50.758 --> 57:51.676
Getting a book.

57:52.343 --> 57:54.137
You ran away from school and went here?

57:55.054 --> 57:56.306
No one would have guessed.

57:57.432 --> 57:58.766
What are you doing here?

58:00.602 --> 58:01.644
They let me off.

58:06.149 --> 58:07.775
Are you reading that book?

58:09.402 --> 58:10.236
Hmm.

58:11.905 --> 58:14.532
Okay, then it might be
a bit difficult for you.

58:14.616 --> 58:16.034
Are you sure you can read it?

58:16.117 --> 58:18.536
That is Nietzsche's
philosophical ideology.

58:18.620 --> 58:20.246
It won't be easy to understand.

58:21.581 --> 58:22.832
THUS SPOKE ZARATHUSTRA

58:24.417 --> 58:27.670
So are you giving me that?
It'll be better if I read it instead.

58:28.546 --> 58:29.839
Eternal recurrence.

58:29.923 --> 58:33.051
It's the concept that
the universe is recurring infinitely.

58:34.385 --> 58:37.096
In eternal recurrence,
all existence is recurring

58:37.180 --> 58:39.724
and will continue
to recur indefinitely forever.

58:39.807 --> 58:43.144
I got curious recently
about the eternity of time.

58:43.228 --> 58:44.437
So I'm reading it again.

58:47.023 --> 58:48.107
[inhales]

58:49.651 --> 58:50.735
Okay.

58:51.402 --> 58:52.737
Return it when you're finished.

58:53.988 --> 58:55.240
About yesterday…

58:56.157 --> 58:57.534
I guess…

58:58.785 --> 59:01.246
I was a bit harsh to you.

59:05.542 --> 59:06.876
Is that why you ran away?

59:07.877 --> 59:09.879
Hmm. I thought you'd be uncomfortable.

59:16.177 --> 59:18.388
I'm hungry. Let's go eat together.

59:18.930 --> 59:21.099
[light cheerful music]

59:21.933 --> 59:28.940
CATCH ME IF YOU CAN

59:50.211 --> 59:52.338
[Ji-ung] Which trip
was the most memorable for you?

59:52.422 --> 59:54.799
[Yeon-su] I think I'm in love with you.

59:54.882 --> 59:57.594
We finally went on another one, huh?
And it's farther.

59:57.677 --> 59:59.596
- I'm very disappointed.
- NJ, hey!

59:59.679 --> 01:00:01.472
[Ji-ung] Gotta say, I'm a little confused.

01:00:01.556 --> 01:00:04.559
I'm wondering if you're showing
all these emotions because…

01:00:04.642 --> 01:00:06.144
[Yeon-su] We're not going to break up.

01:00:07.103 --> 01:00:08.896
Just come to me like you did today.
